# Mobile (`apps/mobile`)

Read ADR-0003 and `docs/specs/45-mobile-ui-kit.md`.

- Routes in `src/app/` (expo-router, default exports, thin, wrapped in `<Screen>`); tabs in
  `src/app/(tabs)/`. Features in `src/features/<feature>/`; primitives in `src/components/ui/`
  (Button, Text, TextField, FormField, Card, ListItem/ListGroup, Banner, Avatar, Divider, Screen).
- Styling: `StyleSheet.create` with `tokens` from `@najme/ui-tokens`; sizes from
  `src/components/ui/theme.ts` (`CONTROL_HEIGHT`, `ICON_SIZE`, `MIN_TOUCH_TARGET`…) — no magic
  numbers. Fonts via `fontFamilies.*` (`fontWeight` does not select custom weights on Android).
- Accessibility role and label on every interactive element; touch targets ≥ 44dp; text scales
  with dynamic type (capped at 1.6x); keyboard avoidance and safe areas via `Screen`.
- API base URL: `process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL` (inlined at bundle time; never a secret). Parse
  responses with contract schemas; time out requests; clean up on unmount.
- Secrets/tokens in `expo-secure-store`, never AsyncStorage. Native-only modules must degrade
  gracefully in Expo Go and in the web export.
- i18n: register namespaces in `src/i18n/index.ts` and `src/test-utils/i18n.tsx`.
- Dev-only screens load through a `__DEV__`-guarded `require`.
- Tests: jest-expo + RNTL (`@jest/globals`, `renderWithI18n`, awaited `render`/`fireEvent`).
- `pnpm --filter @najme/mobile build` (`expo export --platform web`) is part of `pnpm check` and
  must keep passing.
